module app.http_runtime_gauntlet
purpose module app.http_runtime_gauntlet "Native HTTP/1.1 adapter conformance harness: every routing, request-read, response-write, multipart, SSE, and middleware edge currently lowered by the reference compiler is exercised here under a test asserting the exact wire-level contract."
moduleOwns app.http_runtime_gauntlet "All 27 route handlers and middleware ops, the webServer routing surface, path-scoped routeTimeout/routeMiddleware bindings, the gauntlet's two capabilities (httpRequestReader, httpResponseWriter), module-scope status constants, the request-timeout budget, and the response-body forwarder declaration on writeTextResponse."
moduleDoesNotOwn app.http_runtime_gauntlet "The native HTTP runtime itself (sem_http_runtime.c lives under SemanticScript/runtime/native_http), the MiddlewareControl built-in enum (auto-registered by semsc per the docs/reference/syntax-inventory.md MiddlewareControl row), and the dispatcher's short-circuit semantics (owned by the runtime; this module only exercises them via shortCircuitProbeMiddleware)."
moduleWarning app.http_runtime_gauntlet "Two routes intentionally exhibit non-default contracts that future agents MUST NOT 'fix' silently: /reflect/required-header-or-fail pins the adapter's null-body 500 failure path via `pinsNullBodyFailurePath requiredHeaderHandler`, and /middleware-short-circuit pins the dispatcher's short-circuit arm via shortCircuitMiddlewareControl. Both behaviors are externally asserted by test_http_runtime_gauntlet.py; remove the pin and you delete coverage."
invariant module app.http_runtime_gauntlet "Every dispatched route either guards nullable http.request* reads with pointer.isNull and returns 400 on absence, OR carries `pinsNullBodyFailurePath OP \"rationale\"` to opt into the legacy null-body 500 contract. The semlint SS3603 rule enforces this split — silence it only by adding the verb, never by deleting the guard."

# rationale: HttpRequest, HttpResponse, and MiddlewareControl are NOT exported
# here even though every handler signature uses them. Per SS2506
# (module.exportedSymbolNotDeclared), exports must be backed by declarations
# in THIS module — those three are compiler-provided (HttpRequest/HttpResponse
# are opaque dependency tokens registered universally by semsc; MiddlewareControl
# is auto-registered by `_register_builtin_middleware_control_enum`). Re-exporting
# them would be re-publishing a contract this module does not own.
exportCapability app.http_runtime_gauntlet httpRequestReader
exportCapability app.http_runtime_gauntlet httpResponseWriter
exportConstant app.http_runtime_gauntlet okStatus
exportConstant app.http_runtime_gauntlet createdStatus
exportConstant app.http_runtime_gauntlet noContentStatus
exportConstant app.http_runtime_gauntlet redirectStatus
exportConstant app.http_runtime_gauntlet badRequestStatus
exportConstant app.http_runtime_gauntlet largeBodyThreshold
exportOperation app.http_runtime_gauntlet indexHandler
exportOperation app.http_runtime_gauntlet healthHandler
exportOperation app.http_runtime_gauntlet methodReflectHandler
exportOperation app.http_runtime_gauntlet pathReflectHandler
exportOperation app.http_runtime_gauntlet headerReflectHandler
exportOperation app.http_runtime_gauntlet requiredHeaderHandler
exportOperation app.http_runtime_gauntlet queryReflectHandler
exportOperation app.http_runtime_gauntlet queryEmptyHandler
exportOperation app.http_runtime_gauntlet queryRepeatHandler
exportOperation app.http_runtime_gauntlet bodyReflectHandler
exportOperation app.http_runtime_gauntlet bodyBytesReflectHandler
exportOperation app.http_runtime_gauntlet bodySizeHandler
exportOperation app.http_runtime_gauntlet multipartTextHandler
exportOperation app.http_runtime_gauntlet multipartFileNameHandler
exportOperation app.http_runtime_gauntlet multipartFileTypeHandler
exportOperation app.http_runtime_gauntlet multipartFileBytesHandler
exportOperation app.http_runtime_gauntlet sseOneEventHandler
exportOperation app.http_runtime_gauntlet capabilitiesOptionsHandler
exportOperation app.http_runtime_gauntlet customContentHandler
exportOperation app.http_runtime_gauntlet redirectHandler
exportOperation app.http_runtime_gauntlet emptyDeleteHandler
exportOperation app.http_runtime_gauntlet patchHandler
exportOperation app.http_runtime_gauntlet shortCircuitProbeHandler
exportOperation app.http_runtime_gauntlet shortCircuitProbeMiddleware
exportOperation app.http_runtime_gauntlet gauntletMiddleware
exportOperation app.http_runtime_gauntlet writeTextResponse
exportOperation app.http_runtime_gauntlet addGauntletHeaders

# rationale: This app deliberately challenges every native HTTP feature the
# reference compiler currently lowers (route dispatch, request reads,
# response writers, multipart parsing, one-shot SSE framing, path-scoped
# middleware). Routes that previously pinned the adapter's null-body 500
# failure path now explicitly guard with pointer.isNull and return 400;
# /reflect/required-header-or-fail is the one route that intentionally
# still pins the legacy 500 contract so the gauntlet keeps coverage of
# that runtime edge. The unguardedHttpInput linter rule is the contract
# enforcer for that split. project / target / runtime live in build.sem;
# this file owns the module's executable contract.

webServer httpRuntimeGauntletServer
purpose operation httpRuntimeGauntletServer "Challenge every currently implemented native HTTP request, response, routing, and middleware edge"
serverHost httpRuntimeGauntletServer "127.0.0.1"
serverPort httpRuntimeGauntletServer 18082
route httpRuntimeGauntletServer GET "/" indexHandler
route httpRuntimeGauntletServer GET "/health" healthHandler
route httpRuntimeGauntletServer GET "/reflect/method" methodReflectHandler
route httpRuntimeGauntletServer GET "/reflect/path" pathReflectHandler
route httpRuntimeGauntletServer GET "/reflect/header" headerReflectHandler
route httpRuntimeGauntletServer GET "/reflect/required-header-or-fail" requiredHeaderHandler
route httpRuntimeGauntletServer GET "/reflect/query" queryReflectHandler
route httpRuntimeGauntletServer GET "/reflect/query-empty" queryEmptyHandler
route httpRuntimeGauntletServer GET "/reflect/query-repeat" queryRepeatHandler
route httpRuntimeGauntletServer POST "/reflect/body" bodyReflectHandler
route httpRuntimeGauntletServer POST "/reflect/body-bytes" bodyBytesReflectHandler
route httpRuntimeGauntletServer POST "/reflect/body-size" bodySizeHandler
route httpRuntimeGauntletServer PUT "/reflect/body-size" bodySizeHandler
route httpRuntimeGauntletServer POST "/multipart/text" multipartTextHandler
route httpRuntimeGauntletServer POST "/multipart/file-name" multipartFileNameHandler
route httpRuntimeGauntletServer POST "/multipart/file-type" multipartFileTypeHandler
route httpRuntimeGauntletServer POST "/multipart/file-bytes" multipartFileBytesHandler
route httpRuntimeGauntletServer GET "/events/one" sseOneEventHandler
route httpRuntimeGauntletServer OPTIONS "/capabilities" capabilitiesOptionsHandler
route httpRuntimeGauntletServer GET "/content/custom" customContentHandler
route httpRuntimeGauntletServer GET "/redirect" redirectHandler
route httpRuntimeGauntletServer DELETE "/empty" emptyDeleteHandler
route httpRuntimeGauntletServer PATCH "/patch" patchHandler
route httpRuntimeGauntletServer GET "/middleware-short-circuit" shortCircuitProbeHandler

timeoutBudget requestTimeoutBudget DurationMilliseconds 2000
purpose operation requestTimeoutBudget "Document the desired per-route timeout budget; the blocking native adapter does not enforce it yet"
# invariant: routeTimeout is metadata-only in the current blocking adapter
# but every route path is still listed so a future preemptive runtime can
# inherit complete coverage without a follow-up sweep. The POST and PUT
# variants of /reflect/body-size share one path entry by adapter design.
routeTimeout httpRuntimeGauntletServer "/" requestTimeoutBudget
routeTimeout httpRuntimeGauntletServer "/health" requestTimeoutBudget
routeTimeout httpRuntimeGauntletServer "/reflect/method" requestTimeoutBudget
routeTimeout httpRuntimeGauntletServer "/reflect/path" requestTimeoutBudget
routeTimeout httpRuntimeGauntletServer "/reflect/header" requestTimeoutBudget
routeTimeout httpRuntimeGauntletServer "/reflect/required-header-or-fail" requestTimeoutBudget
routeTimeout httpRuntimeGauntletServer "/reflect/query" requestTimeoutBudget
routeTimeout httpRuntimeGauntletServer "/reflect/query-empty" requestTimeoutBudget
routeTimeout httpRuntimeGauntletServer "/reflect/query-repeat" requestTimeoutBudget
routeTimeout httpRuntimeGauntletServer "/reflect/body" requestTimeoutBudget
routeTimeout httpRuntimeGauntletServer "/reflect/body-bytes" requestTimeoutBudget
routeTimeout httpRuntimeGauntletServer "/reflect/body-size" requestTimeoutBudget
routeTimeout httpRuntimeGauntletServer "/multipart/text" requestTimeoutBudget
routeTimeout httpRuntimeGauntletServer "/multipart/file-name" requestTimeoutBudget
routeTimeout httpRuntimeGauntletServer "/multipart/file-type" requestTimeoutBudget
routeTimeout httpRuntimeGauntletServer "/multipart/file-bytes" requestTimeoutBudget
routeTimeout httpRuntimeGauntletServer "/events/one" requestTimeoutBudget
routeTimeout httpRuntimeGauntletServer "/capabilities" requestTimeoutBudget
routeTimeout httpRuntimeGauntletServer "/content/custom" requestTimeoutBudget
routeTimeout httpRuntimeGauntletServer "/redirect" requestTimeoutBudget
routeTimeout httpRuntimeGauntletServer "/empty" requestTimeoutBudget
routeTimeout httpRuntimeGauntletServer "/patch" requestTimeoutBudget
routeTimeout httpRuntimeGauntletServer "/middleware-short-circuit" requestTimeoutBudget
# invariant: routeMiddleware is path-scoped AND now actually executes —
# semsc.py wires the middleware function pointer into the dispatcher so
# gauntletMiddleware fires before each handler. The
# middlewareMissingResponseEffect lint rule enforces that any op bound
# here declares `write http.response*`.
routeMiddleware httpRuntimeGauntletServer "/" gauntletMiddleware
routeMiddleware httpRuntimeGauntletServer "/health" gauntletMiddleware
routeMiddleware httpRuntimeGauntletServer "/reflect/method" gauntletMiddleware
routeMiddleware httpRuntimeGauntletServer "/reflect/path" gauntletMiddleware
routeMiddleware httpRuntimeGauntletServer "/reflect/header" gauntletMiddleware
routeMiddleware httpRuntimeGauntletServer "/reflect/required-header-or-fail" gauntletMiddleware
routeMiddleware httpRuntimeGauntletServer "/reflect/query" gauntletMiddleware
routeMiddleware httpRuntimeGauntletServer "/reflect/query-empty" gauntletMiddleware
routeMiddleware httpRuntimeGauntletServer "/reflect/query-repeat" gauntletMiddleware
routeMiddleware httpRuntimeGauntletServer "/reflect/body" gauntletMiddleware
routeMiddleware httpRuntimeGauntletServer "/reflect/body-bytes" gauntletMiddleware
routeMiddleware httpRuntimeGauntletServer "/reflect/body-size" gauntletMiddleware
routeMiddleware httpRuntimeGauntletServer "/multipart/text" gauntletMiddleware
routeMiddleware httpRuntimeGauntletServer "/multipart/file-name" gauntletMiddleware
routeMiddleware httpRuntimeGauntletServer "/multipart/file-type" gauntletMiddleware
routeMiddleware httpRuntimeGauntletServer "/multipart/file-bytes" gauntletMiddleware
routeMiddleware httpRuntimeGauntletServer "/events/one" gauntletMiddleware
routeMiddleware httpRuntimeGauntletServer "/capabilities" gauntletMiddleware
routeMiddleware httpRuntimeGauntletServer "/content/custom" gauntletMiddleware
routeMiddleware httpRuntimeGauntletServer "/redirect" gauntletMiddleware
routeMiddleware httpRuntimeGauntletServer "/empty" gauntletMiddleware
routeMiddleware httpRuntimeGauntletServer "/patch" gauntletMiddleware
routeMiddleware httpRuntimeGauntletServer "/middleware-short-circuit" shortCircuitProbeMiddleware

capability httpRequestReader http.request read
purpose operation httpRequestReader "Authority to inspect current request method, path, header, query, body, and multipart values"
# invariant: Capability paths are hierarchical: a single `http.request read`
# grant authorizes every narrower `http.request.method`,
# `http.request.path`, `http.request.header`, `http.request.query`,
# `http.request.body`, and `http.request.multipart` read declared by
# downstream handlers. semsc's _check_effect_authority_coverage walks this
# hierarchy via _effect_path_covers.
capability httpResponseWriter http.response write
purpose operation httpResponseWriter "Authority to write status, body, content type, and custom response headers"

# Module-scope status constants — hoisted via `storage module immutable`
# (the canonical replacement for `const NAME TYPE VALUE`). Each value is
# named after the HTTP status code's contract so reviewers see intent at
# the call site, not just a magic number.
storage module immutable okStatus Int32 200
storage module immutable createdStatus Int32 201
storage module immutable noContentStatus Int32 204
storage module immutable redirectStatus Int32 302
storage module immutable badRequestStatus Int32 400
# The body-size threshold is picked so the small test fixture "small"
# (5 bytes) reports as `small body` and the large fixture
# "0123456789abcdef" (16 bytes) reports as `large body`. ByteCount lowers
# as i64 for the math.greaterThanOrEqualInt64 comparison below.
storage module immutable largeBodyThreshold ByteCount 12
purpose operation largeBodyThreshold "Split body-size tests between the small fixture `small` and the large fixture `0123456789abcdef`"

operation addGauntletHeaders
input operation addGauntletHeaders response HttpResponse
output operation addGauntletHeaders Void
effect addGauntletHeaders write http.response
memory addGauntletHeaders arena request
async addGauntletHeaders no
useCapability addGauntletHeaders httpResponseWriter
purpose operation addGauntletHeaders "Attach common response headers (X-Gauntlet-App, X-Gauntlet-Version) used by every gauntlet test for cross-route identification"
invariant operation addGauntletHeaders "All header names and values are static module-scope strings; the native http.responseHeader writer accepts them without copying or escaping. The op returns Void because there is no caller-actionable status — header write failure surfaces at the per-route test assertions, not at this call boundary."
warning addGauntletHeaders "Per-header write statuses (from http.responseHeader) are intentionally ignored — the ignoreValue lines below acknowledge the per-call discard semantically. The op's Void output is the matching caller-side contract: callers do not need an ignoreValue line because Void has no value to discard. If a future http.responseHeader contract grows a caller-actionable failure mode, both the per-call ignoreValue here AND the op output type must be widened together."

label startAddGauntletHeaders

storage local immutable appHeaderName String "X-Gauntlet-App"
storage local immutable appHeaderValue String "http-runtime-gauntlet"
call appHeaderCall http.responseHeader
argument appHeaderCall response HttpResponse response
argument appHeaderCall name String appHeaderName
argument appHeaderCall value String appHeaderValue
run appHeaderCall
ignore value source appHeaderCall type Int32

storage local immutable versionHeaderName String "X-Gauntlet-Version"
storage local immutable versionHeaderValue String "1"
call versionHeaderCall http.responseHeader
argument versionHeaderCall response HttpResponse response
argument versionHeaderCall name String versionHeaderName
argument versionHeaderCall value String versionHeaderValue
run versionHeaderCall
ignore value source versionHeaderCall type Int32

# `returnVoid` is the explicit "no caller-actionable status" return form
# matching this op's `output addGauntletHeaders Void` declaration. Codegen
# lowers it to the i32 zero sentinel expected by the user-op ABI, but the
# source says exactly what it means — no fake-status const that a reader
# would have to recognise as a Void-ABI quirk.
return void

operation writeTextResponse
input operation writeTextResponse response HttpResponse
input operation writeTextResponse status Int32
input operation writeTextResponse body String
output operation writeTextResponse Int32
effect writeTextResponse write http.response
memory writeTextResponse arena request
async writeTextResponse no
useCapability writeTextResponse httpResponseWriter
purpose operation writeTextResponse "Write a plain text response through the native HTTP adapter, with the gauntlet's common headers attached first"
invariant operation writeTextResponse "The body argument is forwarded unchanged to http.responseText; the caller is responsible for ensuring it is non-null. The responseBodyForwarder declaration below tells semlint SS3603 to treat callers of this helper the same as callers of http.responseText, so the null-guard contract is preserved across the wrapper layer rather than relying on a `body` arg-name string match."
responseBodyForwarder writeTextResponse body

label startWriteTextResponse

# rationale: common headers go first because the native adapter latches
# headers into the wire buffer at the first body write — adding them after
# http.responseText would silently lose them.
call commonHeaderCall addGauntletHeaders
argument commonHeaderCall response HttpResponse response
run commonHeaderCall

call writeTextResponseCall http.responseText
argument writeTextResponseCall response HttpResponse response
argument writeTextResponseCall status Int32 status
argument writeTextResponseCall body String body
run writeTextResponseCall
bind value writeTextResponseStatus Int32 writeTextResponseCall
return value writeTextResponseStatus

operation indexHandler
input operation indexHandler request HttpRequest
input operation indexHandler response HttpResponse
output operation indexHandler Int32
effect indexHandler write http.response
memory indexHandler arena request
async indexHandler no
useCapability indexHandler httpResponseWriter
purpose operation indexHandler "Return a compact route map for the HTTP Runtime Gauntlet so operators and tests can discover the surface without out-of-band docs"
invariant operation indexHandler "The route map lists every current API family covered by this demo. The trailing note distinguishes the 400-on-missing-input contract used by most reflect routes from the one route that still pins the legacy null-body 500 contract."

label startIndexHandler

storage local immutable indexBody String "http api gauntlet\nroutes: /health /reflect/method /reflect/path /reflect/header /reflect/required-header-or-fail /reflect/query /reflect/query-empty /reflect/query-repeat /reflect/body /reflect/body-bytes /reflect/body-size /multipart/text /multipart/file-name /multipart/file-type /multipart/file-bytes /events/one /capabilities /content/custom /redirect /empty /patch /middleware-short-circuit\nmissing-input routes respond 400; /reflect/required-header-or-fail intentionally still 500s on missing X-Gauntlet-Required; /middleware-short-circuit returns 418 from its middleware (the route's handler is intentionally skipped by the MiddlewareControl short-circuit contract)\n"
call indexResponseCall writeTextResponse
argument indexResponseCall response HttpResponse response
argument indexResponseCall status Int32 okStatus
argument indexResponseCall body String indexBody
run indexResponseCall
bind value indexResponseStatus Int32 indexResponseCall
return value indexResponseStatus

operation healthHandler
input operation healthHandler request HttpRequest
input operation healthHandler response HttpResponse
output operation healthHandler Int32
effect healthHandler write http.response
memory healthHandler arena request
async healthHandler no
useCapability healthHandler httpResponseWriter
purpose operation healthHandler "Return a minimal readiness body so external probes (tests, orchestrators) can poll for server liveness"
invariant operation healthHandler "Readiness stays static and side-effect free; the probe loop in test_http_runtime_gauntlet.py polls this endpoint until status 200, body `ok\\n`, and X-Gauntlet-App appear together"

label startHealthHandler

storage local immutable healthBody String "ok\n"
call healthResponseCall writeTextResponse
argument healthResponseCall response HttpResponse response
argument healthResponseCall status Int32 okStatus
argument healthResponseCall body String healthBody
run healthResponseCall
bind value healthResponseStatus Int32 healthResponseCall
return value healthResponseStatus

operation methodReflectHandler
input operation methodReflectHandler request HttpRequest
input operation methodReflectHandler response HttpResponse
output operation methodReflectHandler Int32
effect methodReflectHandler read http.request.method
effect methodReflectHandler write http.response
memory methodReflectHandler arena request
async methodReflectHandler no
useCapability methodReflectHandler httpRequestReader
useCapability methodReflectHandler httpResponseWriter
purpose operation methodReflectHandler "Return the exact request method string seen by the adapter so tests can verify case-preservation and exotic-method handling"
invariant operation methodReflectHandler "The adapter method matcher is case-insensitive at dispatch time but http.requestMethod returns the original spelling. The function never returns a null pointer for a dispatched request, so this handler does not need a pointer.isNull guard — every request that reached the handler has a method string."

label startMethodReflectHandler

call methodReadCall http.requestMethod
argument methodReadCall request HttpRequest request
run methodReadCall
bind value requestMethod String methodReadCall
call methodResponseCall writeTextResponse
argument methodResponseCall response HttpResponse response
argument methodResponseCall status Int32 okStatus
argument methodResponseCall body String requestMethod
run methodResponseCall
bind value methodResponseStatus Int32 methodResponseCall
return value methodResponseStatus

operation pathReflectHandler
input operation pathReflectHandler request HttpRequest
input operation pathReflectHandler response HttpResponse
output operation pathReflectHandler Int32
effect pathReflectHandler read http.request.path
effect pathReflectHandler write http.response
memory pathReflectHandler arena request
async pathReflectHandler no
useCapability pathReflectHandler httpRequestReader
useCapability pathReflectHandler httpResponseWriter
purpose operation pathReflectHandler "Return the route path after query stripping so tests can verify the adapter's path normalization"
invariant operation pathReflectHandler "The returned path excludes the query string; http.requestPath returns a non-null pointer for any dispatched request (mirror of http.requestMethod), so no null guard is needed here"

label startPathReflectHandler

call pathReadCall http.requestPath
argument pathReadCall request HttpRequest request
run pathReadCall
bind value requestPath String pathReadCall
call pathResponseCall writeTextResponse
argument pathResponseCall response HttpResponse response
argument pathResponseCall status Int32 okStatus
argument pathResponseCall body String requestPath
run pathResponseCall
bind value pathResponseStatus Int32 pathResponseCall
return value pathResponseStatus

operation headerReflectHandler
input operation headerReflectHandler request HttpRequest
input operation headerReflectHandler response HttpResponse
output operation headerReflectHandler Int32
effect headerReflectHandler read http.request.header
effect headerReflectHandler write http.response
memory headerReflectHandler arena request
async headerReflectHandler no
useCapability headerReflectHandler httpRequestReader
useCapability headerReflectHandler httpResponseWriter
purpose operation headerReflectHandler "Return the case-insensitive X-Gauntlet-Token request header when present, or a 400 with a static reason body when absent"
invariant operation headerReflectHandler "X-Gauntlet-Token absent ⇒ http.requestHeader returns null ⇒ pointer.isNull guard branches to headerMissingPath ⇒ 400. Present ⇒ raw header value returned with status 200. This route does NOT pin the null-body 500 contract; that role belongs to requiredHeaderHandler."
warning headerReflectHandler "The 400-on-missing-token contract is part of the route's tested surface; scripts/check_http_runtime_gauntlet.ps1 asserts the 400 response body matches `missing header: X-Gauntlet-Token\\n`. Do not silently switch this back to the null-body 500 path — requiredHeaderHandler exists specifically to keep that coverage."

label startHeaderReflectHandler

storage local immutable tokenHeaderName String "x-gauntlet-token"
storage local immutable tokenMissingBody String "missing header: X-Gauntlet-Token\n"
call headerReadCall http.requestHeader
argument headerReadCall request HttpRequest request
argument headerReadCall name String tokenHeaderName
run headerReadCall
bind value tokenHeaderValue String headerReadCall

rationale tokenMissingCheckCall "pointer.isNull is the only typed null detector — the default branchIfError convention (result < 0) cannot inspect a returned NULL pointer. semsc's pointer.isNull lowering emits a real `icmp_unsigned eq ptr, null` so the branchIf below has a real Bool to read. The rationale is attached to the call via SS3608 instead of a proximity `# rationale:` comment so a refactor that renames or removes the call also surfaces this context as orphaned."
call tokenMissingCheckCall pointer.isNull
argument tokenMissingCheckCall pointer OpaquePointer tokenHeaderValue
run tokenMissingCheckCall
bind value tokenMissing Bool tokenMissingCheckCall
branch if condition tokenMissing target headerMissingPath

call headerResponseCall writeTextResponse
argument headerResponseCall response HttpResponse response
argument headerResponseCall status Int32 okStatus
argument headerResponseCall body String tokenHeaderValue
run headerResponseCall
bind value headerResponseStatus Int32 headerResponseCall
return value headerResponseStatus

label headerMissingPath
call headerMissingResponseCall writeTextResponse
argument headerMissingResponseCall response HttpResponse response
argument headerMissingResponseCall status Int32 badRequestStatus
argument headerMissingResponseCall body String tokenMissingBody
run headerMissingResponseCall
bind value headerMissingResponseStatus Int32 headerMissingResponseCall
return value headerMissingResponseStatus

operation requiredHeaderHandler
input operation requiredHeaderHandler request HttpRequest
input operation requiredHeaderHandler response HttpResponse
output operation requiredHeaderHandler Int32
effect requiredHeaderHandler read http.request.header
effect requiredHeaderHandler write http.response
memory requiredHeaderHandler arena request
async requiredHeaderHandler no
useCapability requiredHeaderHandler httpRequestReader
useCapability requiredHeaderHandler httpResponseWriter
purpose operation requiredHeaderHandler "Negative-test route: returns the required header value with 200 when X-Gauntlet-Required is present, and intentionally exposes the adapter's null-body 500 failure path when absent"
invariant operation requiredHeaderHandler "This is the gauntlet's one route that intentionally omits a pointer.isNull guard. The absent-header case binds null to requiredHeaderValue, passes it to writeTextResponse → http.responseText, and the runtime rejects the null body with a 500. This pins the adapter's `handler failed` contract for regression detection."
pinsNullBodyFailurePath requiredHeaderHandler "The /reflect/required-header-or-fail route is the gauntlet's deliberate coverage of the adapter's null-body 500 path. semlint SS3603 treats the presence of this verb as the canonical opt-out; the rationale string here documents WHY the route is shaped this way so a future agent removing the verb has to first prove the runtime contract has changed and the coverage is no longer needed."
warning requiredHeaderHandler "Do not add a pointer.isNull guard to this handler. The 500-on-missing-X-Gauntlet-Required behavior is asserted by the `required_missing_headers` block of `test_http_runtime_gauntlet.py` (grep for `/reflect/required-header-or-fail` to find the assertion) as the gauntlet's only check that the native adapter still returns `handler failed\\n` when a handler hands a null body to http.responseText. If the runtime contract for null bodies changes, update both the test and this op together — do not silence the assertion by adding a guard here."

label startRequiredHeaderHandler

storage local immutable requiredHeaderName String "x-gauntlet-required"
call requiredHeaderReadCall http.requestHeader
argument requiredHeaderReadCall request HttpRequest request
argument requiredHeaderReadCall name String requiredHeaderName
run requiredHeaderReadCall
bind value requiredHeaderValue String requiredHeaderReadCall
call requiredHeaderResponseCall writeTextResponse
argument requiredHeaderResponseCall response HttpResponse response
argument requiredHeaderResponseCall status Int32 okStatus
argument requiredHeaderResponseCall body String requiredHeaderValue
run requiredHeaderResponseCall
bind value requiredHeaderResponseStatus Int32 requiredHeaderResponseCall
return value requiredHeaderResponseStatus

operation queryReflectHandler
input operation queryReflectHandler request HttpRequest
input operation queryReflectHandler response HttpResponse
output operation queryReflectHandler Int32
effect queryReflectHandler read http.request.query
effect queryReflectHandler write http.response
memory queryReflectHandler arena request
async queryReflectHandler no
useCapability queryReflectHandler httpRequestReader
useCapability queryReflectHandler httpResponseWriter
purpose operation queryReflectHandler "Return the raw `name` query parameter when present, or a 400 with a static reason body when absent"
invariant operation queryReflectHandler "Query values are raw, undecoded splits — percent-decoding is intentionally future work. The guard distinguishes `?name=foo` (returned verbatim, 200) from `?other=foo` or no query string (null bind ⇒ 400) and from `?name=` (empty string bind, 200)."
warning queryReflectHandler "The 400-on-missing-name contract is tested externally; if the request omits `name` the response body is `missing query parameter: name\\n`. Refactors that switch this back to the null-body 500 path break the test."

label startQueryReflectHandler

storage local immutable nameQueryName String "name"
storage local immutable nameQueryMissingBody String "missing query parameter: name\n"
call queryReadCall http.requestQueryParam
argument queryReadCall request HttpRequest request
argument queryReadCall name String nameQueryName
run queryReadCall
bind value queryValue String queryReadCall

# rationale: same null-guard pattern as headerReflectHandler — keeps the
# 400 contract for absent keys distinct from the empty-value contract
# exercised by queryEmptyHandler.
call queryMissingCheckCall pointer.isNull
argument queryMissingCheckCall pointer OpaquePointer queryValue
run queryMissingCheckCall
bind value queryMissing Bool queryMissingCheckCall
branch if condition queryMissing target queryReflectMissingPath

call queryResponseCall writeTextResponse
argument queryResponseCall response HttpResponse response
argument queryResponseCall status Int32 okStatus
argument queryResponseCall body String queryValue
run queryResponseCall
bind value queryResponseStatus Int32 queryResponseCall
return value queryResponseStatus

label queryReflectMissingPath
call queryReflectMissingResponseCall writeTextResponse
argument queryReflectMissingResponseCall response HttpResponse response
argument queryReflectMissingResponseCall status Int32 badRequestStatus
argument queryReflectMissingResponseCall body String nameQueryMissingBody
run queryReflectMissingResponseCall
bind value queryReflectMissingResponseStatus Int32 queryReflectMissingResponseCall
return value queryReflectMissingResponseStatus

operation queryEmptyHandler
input operation queryEmptyHandler request HttpRequest
input operation queryEmptyHandler response HttpResponse
output operation queryEmptyHandler Int32
effect queryEmptyHandler read http.request.query
effect queryEmptyHandler write http.response
memory queryEmptyHandler arena request
async queryEmptyHandler no
useCapability queryEmptyHandler httpRequestReader
useCapability queryEmptyHandler httpResponseWriter
purpose operation queryEmptyHandler "Return the empty value for a query key that has no equals sign (?empty), or 400 when the key is absent entirely"
invariant operation queryEmptyHandler "Three distinct cases: `?empty` → empty string bind → 200 with empty body; `?empty=value` → `value` bind → 200; no `empty` at all → null bind → 400. The native query splitter treats a key without `=` as having an empty-string value, which is the case under test."
warning queryEmptyHandler "Do not collapse the absent-key and present-with-empty-value cases: tests rely on the 200/empty-body distinction to verify the native splitter's `key-without-equals` behavior. Tests also rely on the 400-on-absent-key contract for regression coverage of the guard pattern."

label startQueryEmptyHandler

storage local immutable emptyQueryName String "empty"
storage local immutable emptyQueryMissingBody String "missing query parameter: empty\n"
call emptyQueryReadCall http.requestQueryParam
argument emptyQueryReadCall request HttpRequest request
argument emptyQueryReadCall name String emptyQueryName
run emptyQueryReadCall
bind value emptyQueryValue String emptyQueryReadCall

call emptyQueryMissingCheckCall pointer.isNull
argument emptyQueryMissingCheckCall pointer OpaquePointer emptyQueryValue
run emptyQueryMissingCheckCall
bind value emptyQueryMissing Bool emptyQueryMissingCheckCall
branch if condition emptyQueryMissing target queryEmptyMissingPath

call emptyQueryResponseCall writeTextResponse
argument emptyQueryResponseCall response HttpResponse response
argument emptyQueryResponseCall status Int32 okStatus
argument emptyQueryResponseCall body String emptyQueryValue
run emptyQueryResponseCall
bind value emptyQueryResponseStatus Int32 emptyQueryResponseCall
return value emptyQueryResponseStatus

label queryEmptyMissingPath
call queryEmptyMissingResponseCall writeTextResponse
argument queryEmptyMissingResponseCall response HttpResponse response
argument queryEmptyMissingResponseCall status Int32 badRequestStatus
