invariant operation sseOneEventHandler "Current native SSE support is one-shot event-stream FORMATTING, not a long-lived streaming connection — the response is sent and the socket closes. Cache-Control: no-cache is added because intermediaries can otherwise cache an event-stream response, defeating the live-event semantics."
warning sseOneEventHandler "Real SSE clients hold the socket open for many events; this handler returns immediately after one event. Tests that expect server-push behavior need a future long-lived response API (tracked under docs/reference/syntax-inventory.md's webServer Partial row)."

