useCapability shortCircuitProbeMiddleware httpResponseWriter
purpose operation shortCircuitProbeMiddleware "Test fixture for the MiddlewareControl short-circuit contract: write a fully-formed response with a teapot-flavoured status, then return shortCircuitMiddlewareControl so sem_http_runtime.c sends the response as-is and skips the route's handler entirely"
invariant operation shortCircuitProbeMiddleware "Returns shortCircuitMiddlewareControl unconditionally. The dispatcher reads the i32 return value and matches it against SS_HTTP_MIDDLEWARE_SHORT_CIRCUIT (= 1) in sem_http_runtime.c. The bound handler (`shortCircuitProbeHandler`) MUST NEVER run when this middleware fires; if a test sees the handler's body, the contract has regressed."
warning shortCircuitProbeMiddleware "Do not bind this middleware to any other route. The `/middleware-short-circuit` route exists solely to exercise the shortCircuitMiddlewareControl arm of the dispatcher contract. Reusing this middleware on a real route would 418 every request."

label startShortCircuitProbeMiddleware

storage local immutable teapotStatus Int32 418
storage local immutable shortCircuitBody String "middleware short-circuited; handler skipped by dispatcher\n"
storage local immutable shortCircuitContentType String "text/plain; charset=utf-8"
call shortCircuitWriteCall http.responseText
argument shortCircuitWriteCall response HttpResponse response
argument shortCircuitWriteCall status Int32 teapotStatus
argument shortCircuitWriteCall body String shortCircuitBody
argument shortCircuitWriteCall contentType HttpContentType shortCircuitContentType
run shortCircuitWriteCall
ignore value source shortCircuitWriteCall type Int32

return value shortCircuitMiddlewareControl

operation gauntletMiddleware
input operation gauntletMiddleware request HttpRequest
input operation gauntletMiddleware response HttpResponse
output operation gauntletMiddleware MiddlewareControl
effect gauntletMiddleware read http.request.path
effect gauntletMiddleware write http.response
memory gauntletMiddleware arena request
async gauntletMiddleware no
useCapability gauntletMiddleware httpRequestReader
useCapability gauntletMiddleware httpResponseWriter
purpose operation gauntletMiddleware "Set diagnostic response headers (X-Gauntlet-Middleware, X-Gauntlet-Path) before each path-scoped route handler runs so the test can verify middleware actually executed and saw the right path"
invariant operation gauntletMiddleware "Middleware runs synchronously before the route handler in the native dispatcher (semsc.py wires the middleware pointer into per-route dispatch; sem_http_runtime.c reads the MiddlewareControl return value). This op always returns `continueMiddlewareControl` so every route's handler runs after the diagnostic headers are stamped. http.requestPath always returns a non-null pointer for any dispatched request so no guard is needed for middlewareRequestPath."
warning gauntletMiddleware "Returning `shortCircuitMiddlewareControl` from any middleware tells the dispatcher to SKIP the route handler and ship the middleware-written response as-is. Do not introduce a short-circuit return here without also writing a complete response (status + body + content-type) — sem_http_runtime.c maps short-circuit with a null body to a 500 with `middleware short-circuited without writing a response\\n` so the dispatcher gap is visible at the client."
warning gauntletMiddleware "The middlewareMissingResponseEffect (SS3602) and middlewareReturnNotMiddlewareControl (SS3610) lint rules enforce the two halves of the routeMiddleware contract: write effect declared, and output typed as MiddlewareControl. If you split this middleware into a read-only variant that does not write headers, that route's middleware binding will start tripping SS3602 until you either add a write effect or rethink whether middleware is the right hook."

label startGauntletMiddleware

storage local immutable middlewareHeaderName String "X-Gauntlet-Middleware"
storage local immutable middlewareHeaderValue String "active"
call middlewareHeaderCall http.responseHeader
argument middlewareHeaderCall response HttpResponse response
argument middlewareHeaderCall name String middlewareHeaderName
argument middlewareHeaderCall value String middlewareHeaderValue
run middlewareHeaderCall
ignore value source middlewareHeaderCall type Int32

call middlewarePathReadCall http.requestPath
argument middlewarePathReadCall request HttpRequest request
run middlewarePathReadCall
bind value middlewareRequestPath String middlewarePathReadCall

storage local immutable middlewarePathHeaderName String "X-Gauntlet-Path"
call middlewarePathHeaderCall http.responseHeader
argument middlewarePathHeaderCall response HttpResponse response
argument middlewarePathHeaderCall name String middlewarePathHeaderName
argument middlewarePathHeaderCall value String middlewareRequestPath
run middlewarePathHeaderCall
ignore value source middlewarePathHeaderCall type Int32

# rationale tokenMissingCheckCall established the pattern: explicit named
# cases are the contract, not bare integer sentinels. continueMiddlewareControl
# is the auto-registered case-0 constant from the built-in MiddlewareControl
# enum (see semsc.py:_register_builtin_middleware_control_enum); returning
# it here tells the dispatcher to fall through to the route handler. A
# returnValue of `shortCircuitMiddlewareControl` would skip the handler.
return value continueMiddlewareControl
